      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-06-15_WidnesExaminer_art0046" n="art0046">
        <head>Are You Run-Down or Rheumatic ?</head>
        <p>Are You Run-Down or Rheumatic ?</p>
        <p>Kidney Trouble Affects the Whole System.</p>
        <p>NOURE loses no time in giving you warning of kidney and bladder trouble. Bsekache, twinges of pain when stooping or lifting, —'4ches, spells of faintness and urinary disorders are 4111" g the first symptoms. If these warnings are unheeded, there comes a steady llssy37aching in the back and loins, a noticeable weak- ness and a loss of flesh, rheumatic attacks, weakening Ot din:lnfest of the sight, irregular action of the heart, attacks of gravel, bladder weakness, dropsical bloating etc,</p>
        <p>Doan's Trickache Kidney Pills have a splendid repute- tlort for the speedy relief and permanent cure of kidney alld bladder diseases. They are compounded of vege- able drugs which have a direct and benefice! action 11130 u the kidneys and urinari system. Warrington "res have long proved the value of Doan's Backache lidney Pills ; here to-day is the record of another %%ae of</p>
        <p>of her kidney trouble by Doan's Backache Kidney Plll5 she said :—" There is no mistake about it, Doan's pills are a splendid medicine, and all that has been published about my cure is quite true. My cure has proved a lasting one, and I can endorse every word I previously said. There has been no return of my oomplaint to speak of, but at times when I catch cold I feel a slight pain, but Doan's pills quickly put me right."</p>
        <p>Mrs. Farrington's original statement is as follows : "For two years I suffered agonies with pains in my back, caused by my kidneys being out of order. The secretion from them was unnatural, my eyes were puffy underneath, am! I came over giddy. I seemed to be fall of wind; my rest did me no good, and I got very feeble. A neighbour told me about Doan's Backache Kidneys Pills, and I got some to try. Gradually I got better until I was quite myself again. My kidneys were acting properly, and the pains and other symptoms had gone. (Signed), A. Farrington."</p>
        <p>Of all chemists and stores 2s. 9d. per box ; 6 boxes 13s. 9d., or post free, direct from Foster McClellan Co., 8, Wells-street, Oxford-street, London, W.</p>
