        <p>WARRINGTON POLICE T. SOUTHPORT POLICE.—On Thursday a main of bowls was played bettveen the members of the above Police Forces, on the Arpley Green, by the kind permission of the members of the Warrington Cricket and Bowling Club, and resulted in a victory for the local Guardians of the Peace by forty- one points. The scores were :</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON. SOUTHPORT Sergt. Barlow 9l P.C. Tetlow ll Act. Sergt. Meacock 9l P.C. Welding P.C. 12, Newey ...... ...... 21 P.C. Liddle 5 P.C. 26, Sankey P.C. 27, Burton P.C. 31, Lewis 2l Sergt. Eastham (Capt.) 11 P.C.:36, Cooper (Capt.) 2l P.C. Hoyle P.C. 44, Cbrimes 2l P.C. Black P.C. 45, Dawson ld P.C. Smith P.C. 49, Tolley P.C. 56, Reddington P.C. 67, Armstrong</p>
        <p>Total 221</p>
        <p>Total 180</p>
        <p>Majority for the Warrington team 41. After the main the visiting team was entertained to a substantial tea, by the locals, and an enjoyable even- ing was spent. The return main at Southport will be anxiously looked forward to by the members of our local Force.</p>
