      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-06-15_WidnesExaminer_art0120" n="art0120">
        <head>RECTOR IN CLOGS.</head>
        <p>A RECTOR IN CLOGS.</p>
        <p>Dr. Mercer, rector of St, Paulinus, near Preston, has charge of a willing flock. Efforts are being made to erect a house, and the rfctor is securing cheap bat willing labour. He acts the part of employer, and his workers are the members of the congregation. Dr. Mercer, attired in old clothes and clogs, is now on the job wielding his pick ani shovel, and inspiring his co-workers.</p>
      </div>
