        <p>"OBTAINED GREAT RELIEF." 63, Sherwood-street, Oxford-read, Reading, October Ist, 190 G. Dear Sir,—l am writidg these lines to you to testify to the value of your Gout Pills. My father, who is now dead, was a great sufferer from Gout, in fact one of the worst sufferers in Reading, where we are well known. My eldest brother is also a chronic sufferer, and I myself suffer from the same complaint. My father and brother OBTAINED GREAT RELIEF from taking your Pills, so it is natural that I should use them, and this I have done for the last five years, and have always found them to almost relieve me at once. lam still using them. Trusting you will not I take offence at this poor letter, I remain, yours truly, J. HOPSON (a working man). EADE'S GOUT PILLS ! Are perfectly safe in their action, eliminate all I jurinus matter, andare highly restorative. ,I Sold everywhere in Bottles, is lid and 2s 9d, or sent I post free for stamps or P.O. by the Proprietor GEORGE EADE, 232, Goswell road, London. a</p>
